 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Save the date cards are really popular for special events like anniversarys and birthdays. Then a nice touch a few weeks ahead gives people a heads up without overpowering calendars. Lots of people still use post office boxes or have change of address cards, so mail is fine. Email is short and sweet, but it lacks the physical touch. Paper save the date sticker and a small box of them costs nearly nothing. Sticker it on with a sharp pen and you' won an eco point. Invites are full blown invitations, just short and simple. A few words about why you want spend that weekend together is nice.",
